// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Wind | per_page=5 | page=47 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T22:30:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Refactor profile config and add OS detection for workbench\n\nRefactor the profile configuration in ResolveConfiguration to use a reusable DefaultProfile variable instead of duplicate inline objects. Add the os configuration object with release (parsed from navigator.userAgent), hostname, and arch (arm64/x86_64 detection) required by the VS Code workbench.\n\nAlso improve IPCRendererShim to handle known no-op vscode: channels (createSharedProcessChannelConnection, toggleDevTools, reloadWindow, etc.) without logging warnings, and return undefined for truly unmapped channels instead of calling non-existent Tauri commands. Add a stub for utilityProcessWorker in TauriMainProcessService to prevent UtilityProcessWorkerWorkbenchService from hanging.\n\nThese changes complete the workbench initialization requirements and reduce noise from expected IPC calls.",
			"SHA": "4788084ce9535bfbf5805b967ce6098d16535ba2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T21:15:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Complete profile URI configuration and improve IPC error handling\n\nAdd missing URI fields to default profile configuration in ResolveConfiguration:\n- location: vscode-userdata scheme for profile directory\n- promptsHome: user prompts path\n- extensionsResource: extensions.json path\n- mcpResource: mcp.json path\n\nThese URI fields were undefined, preventing the VS Code workbench from locating user data directories.\n\nAlso improve TauriMainProcessService error handling:\n- Add storage stub (getItems, updateItems, optimize, isUsed) to prevent NativeWorkbenchStorageService from hanging\n- Return undefined on IPC failures instead of throwing, since many services don't handle rejections gracefully\n- Change console.error to console.warn for failed channel calls\n\nThese changes enable the workbench to initialize properly and make IPC more resilient to service errors.",
			"SHA": "5ad4d3c96f4b84405c4b1bc5022a1503062fff62"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T16:13:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				20
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Tauri 2.x invoke compatibility across all polyfills\n\nUpdate Tauri invoke calls in all Wind polyfills and services to support both Tauri 1.x and 2.x APIs. The invoke pattern changed from `window.__TAURI__.invoke()` (Tauri 1.x) to `window.__TAURI__.core.invoke()` (Tauri 2.x).\n\nChanges:\n- Update invokeTauri() in: ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill, SharedProcessProxy\n- Update InvokeMountain() in TauriMainProcessService\n- Add TelemetryLive layer to Bootstrap configuration\n- Reorganize TextModelResolver import in Tauri.ts layer\n\nAll polyfills now check for Tauri 2.x first (core.invoke), then fall back to 1.x patterns, ensuring backward compatibility with existing Tauri 1.x deployments while enabling Tauri 2.x upgrades.",
			"SHA": "14c15166326ad501986bc36dbd49f45458ff6779"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-08T13:01:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1022,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add Tauri-native IPC routing and complete workbench configuration\n\nImplement two parallel IPC pathways to replace Electron's ipcMain:\n\n1. **IPCRendererShim binary protocol loopback**: Re-implement VS Code's binary IPC serialization (SerializeIPC/DeserializeIPC) to handle vscode:message events with loopback responses. Provides stub handlers for channels (logger, storage, configuration, localFilesystem) to prevent workbench hangs.\n\n2. **TauriMainProcessService**: New drop-in replacement for ElectronIPCMainProcessService that routes channel.call() directly through Tauri invoke to Mountain's WindServiceHandlers. Eliminates binary protocol overhead entirely - uses plain JSON over Tauri commands.\n\n3. **ResolveConfiguration**: Extend with full INativeWindowConfiguration including profiles, colorScheme, accessibilitySupport, and other DesktopMain fields. Also fix appRoot to strip origin (workbench prepends vscode-file://), and set VSCODE_DEV: \"true\" for relative imports.\n\nThis enables the VS Code workbench to initialize in the Tauri webview with either protocol path.",
			"SHA": "19bbd809f09ee8f7a5602026ec86e8eccab12a81"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
